t = \frac{15 \pm \sqrt{(-15)^2 - 4 \cdot 4 \cdot 14}}{2 \cdot 4} = \frac{15 \pm \sqrt{225 - 224}}{8} = \frac{15 \pm \sqrt{1}}{8} = \frac{15 \pm 1}{8}
\] So the solutions are \( t = \frac{16}{8} = 2 \) and \( t = \frac{14}{8} = 1.75 \). The projectile first reaches 56 feet at \( t = 1.75 \) seconds. </think> <answer> 1.75 </answer>

